WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.628
General chat models provide broad assistance.

00:00:02.628 --> 00:00:04.734
Coding models emphasize software tasks.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:08.526
Reasoning-oriented models may spend more time on complex problems.

00:00:08.526 --> 00:00:11.896
Embedding models convert text into vectors for retrieval.

00:00:11.896 --> 00:00:15.266
Vision-language models process images as well as text.

00:00:15.266 --> 00:00:20.322
Select models by task tests, language needs, context, license, provenance, runtime support,

00:00:20.322 --> 00:00:22.428
memory, latency, and error behavior.

00:00:22.428 --> 00:00:28.326
A larger model may improve difficult work while making ordinary interaction slow or expensive.

00:00:28.326 --> 00:00:32.539
Quantization reduces numerical precision to lower memory and compute requirements.

00:00:32.539 --> 00:00:35.488
Quality tradeoffs vary by model and task.

00:00:35.488 --> 00:00:42.229
Compare several practical quantizations instead of assuming the highest precision is always the best system choice.

00:00:42.229 --> 00:00:45.599
Ollama and LM Studio simplify common local workflows.

00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:46.249
llama.

00:00:46.249 --> 00:00:49.198
cpp provides lower-level control for compatible models.

00:00:49.198 --> 00:00:54.254
Open WebUI offers a web interface that can connect to supported services.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:57.624
API-compatible servers help applications integrate with local inference.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:01.837
Runtime choice affects model formats, drivers, acceleration, context, batching, concurrency,

00:01:01.837 --> 00:01:03.522
logging, APIs, and security.

00:01:03.522 --> 00:01:08.577
A model that works in one tool may behave differently in another

00:01:08.577 --> 00:01:11.526
because prompt templates and generation defaults change.

00:01:11.526 --> 00:01:15.739
Shortlist a few complete configurations and evaluate them before committing.

00:01:15.739 --> 00:01:19.952
Record model, file, quantization, runtime, backend, prompt template, settings, hardware,

00:01:19.952 --> 00:01:20.795
and date.

00:01:20.795 --> 00:01:24.586
Treat model upgrades as application changes, not transparent replacements.

00:01:24.586 --> 00:01:29.642
A model-routing or fallback policy can assign simple work to a small

00:01:29.642 --> 00:01:34.697
local model and escalate difficult requests to an approved stronger service or

00:01:34.697 --> 00:01:35.347
human.

00:01:35.347 --> 00:01:38.260
Routing must honor data classification and user expectations.
